# 2. Port Mapping

```bash
docker run -d -p 8080:80 nginx
```

Meaning:

```text
Host Port : Container Port
8080      : 80
```

Flow:

```text
Browser
   |
   | http://localhost:8080
   v
Host Port 8080
   |
   v
Container Port 80
   |
   v
Nginx
```

The application listens on port `80` inside the container, while users access it through port `8080` on the host.

