# 17. Docker Cleanup

### Remove Stopped Containers

```bash
docker container prune
```

### Remove Unused Images

```bash
docker image prune
```

### Remove Unused Volumes

```bash
docker volume prune
```

### Remove Unused Networks

```bash
docker network prune
```

### Remove Unused Docker Resources

```bash
docker system prune
```

### More Aggressive Cleanup

```bash
docker system prune -a
```

> ⚠️ Be careful because cleanup commands can remove Docker resources that are no longer referenced but may still be needed later.

